DOCUMENT();
loadMacros(
"PGstandard.pl",
"MathObjects.pl",
"PGML.pl"
);
Context("Numeric");
Context()->flags->set(reduceConstantFunctions=>0);
Context()->flags->set(reduceConstants=>0);

$fun_2 = Formula("(e^(x))/7");
$fun_1 = Formula("(((x)^(1/3)))^2");

Context("Interval");

$set_ans_3 = Compute("((((-infinity, 19))) U {-7, -6, -1, 1} U ({-7, -6, -1, 1})) - ((-infinity, infinity) - {-7, -6, -1, 1}) - ((-infinity, infinity) - (-infinity, 19))");
$set_ans_4 = Compute("(-infinity, 13] U (((-infinity, 19))) U (-infinity, 13] - ((-infinity, infinity) - (({-7, -6, -1, 1}) U {-7, -6, -1, 1}))");
$set_ans_5 = Compute("{-7, -6, -1, 1} - ((-infinity, infinity) - (-infinity, 13]) U (-infinity, 13]");
$set_ans_1 = Compute("(9, infinity) - ((-infinity, infinity) - {-10, -3, 0, 1, 2}) U (9, infinity)");
$set_ans_2 = Compute("(9, infinity) U ({-1, 0, 5} U (9, infinity))");

Context("Vector");

BEGIN_PGML
# Questions:

_For arithmetic problems, if the result is not an integer, then retain *three significant digits*._

What is the value of [`13/17+0*3`]? [_____]{answer=>0.764705882353,width=>1}
---

What is the value of [`17+5-9+3*2`]? [_____]{answer=>19,width=>8}
---

Given the sets:
- [`A = \{-1, 0, 5\}`]
- [`B = \{-10, -3, 0, 1, 2\}`]
- [`C = \{x | x > 8\}`]

Compute:
- [`C \cap B \cup C = `] [_____]{$set_ans_1}
- [`C \cup (A \cup C) = `] [_____]{$set_ans_2}

---

Given the sets:
- [`A = \{-7, -6, -1, 1\}`]
- [`B = \{x | x \leq 13\}`]
- [`C = \{x | x < 19\}`]

Compute:
- [`(((C)) \cup A \cup (A)) \cap A \cap C = `] [_____]{$set_ans_3}
- [`B \cup ((C)) \cup B \cap ((A) \cup A) = `] [_____]{$set_ans_4}
- [`A \cap B \cup B = `] [_____]{$set_ans_5}

---

Suppose the vectors:
- [` \vec{u} = \langle -10, 0, -9 \rangle `]
- [` \vec{v} = \langle 4, 2, 10 \rangle `]

Compute:
- [` \left\| \vec{u} \right\| = `] [_____]{norm(Compute("<-10, 0, -9>"))}
- [` \vec{v} \cdot \vec{u} = `] [_____]{Compute("<4, 2, 10>") . Compute("<-10, 0, -9>")}
- Enter a vector in the same direction as [` \vec{v} `]. [_____]{Compute("<4, 2, 10>")->cmp(parallel=>1,sameDirection=>1)}
- [` \vec{u} \times \vec{v} = `] [_____]{Compute("<-10, 0, -9>") x Compute("<4, 2, 10>")}
- Enter a vector in the same direction as [` \vec{u} `]. [_____]{Compute("<-10, 0, -9>")->cmp(parallel=>1,sameDirection=>1)}
- Enter a unit vector in the direction of [` \vec{u} `]. [_____]{unit(Compute("<-10, 0, -9>"))}

---

Suppose the vectors:
- [` \vec{u} = \langle -2, 7, -5 \rangle `]
- [` \vec{v} = \langle -5, 5, -6 \rangle `]
- [` \vec{w} = \langle 9, -10, 5 \rangle `]

Compute:
- [` \left\| \vec{v} \right\| = `] [_____]{norm(Compute("<-5, 5, -6>"))}
- [` \vec{w} \cdot \vec{v} = `] [_____]{Compute("<9, -10, 5>") . Compute("<-5, 5, -6>")}
- [` \left\| \vec{u} \right\| = `] [_____]{norm(Compute("<-2, 7, -5>"))}
- [` \vec{v} \cdot \vec{u} = `] [_____]{Compute("<-5, 5, -6>") . Compute("<-2, 7, -5>")}
- Enter a vector parallel to [` \vec{v} `]. [_____]{Compute("<-5, 5, -6>")->cmp(parallel=>1)}

---

Given this function:

>> [`[$fun_1]`] <<

Compute:
- [`f'(x) =`] [_____]{$fun_1->D()}
- [`f''(x) =`] [_____]{$fun_1->D()->D()}
- [`f'(6) =`] [_____]{$fun_1->D()->eval(x=>6)}

---

Given this function:

>> [`[$fun_2]`] <<

Compute:
- [`f'(x) =`] [_____]{$fun_2->D()}
- [`f'(7) =`] [_____]{$fun_2->D()->eval(x=>7)}
- [`f''(x) =`] [_____]{$fun_2->D()->D()}
- [`f'(1) =`] [_____]{$fun_2->D()->eval(x=>1)}

---
END_PGML
ENDDOCUMENT();
